# 2026-07-31 11:07:18.158753
+Create validate_burn.py. Flat script.
+
+Uniform slab s in [0,1]: j = [1, 0.7, 0, 0] everywhere, rho_V = 2 * PHI * lam2 everywhere, PHI = 10.0, no absorption. Sweep lam2 from 0.001 to 0.5 in 60 log-spaced points. For each: integrate, compute polarization fraction p = sqrt(Q^2+U^2)/I and chi = 0.5*arctan2(U,Q) at s=1.
+
+Exact theory: p/p0 = |sin(PHI*lam2)/(PHI*lam2)| with p0 = 0.7, and chi = 0.5*PHI*lam2 (mod pi ambiguity).
+
+Print a table: lam2, p_numeric, p_theory, chi_numeric, chi_theory. PASS criteria:
+1. max relative error of p vs theory < 0.5% away from the nulls.
+2. First depolarization null at lam2 = pi/10 = 0.3142.
+3. At lam2 = pi/20: p/p0 = 0.6366 within 0.5%.
+4. chi slope = 5.0 (HALF the external-screen slope from validate_screen.py) within 0.1%.
+
+Also save a plot p vs lam2, numeric points over theory curve, matplotlib only.

